(3145837, 439053, 48471, '<td valign="top">4 the only interesting thing about this photo is the depth of field, which doesn´t say much about the quality. not only that this is quite a boring photo of some money (what´s the point of this money being there? where did it come from? whose is it? - questions i´m not interested at all finding the answers), but even technically this photo leaves to be desired. i guess a way to improve it would be playing with colour and saturation, or having a less uniform and dull lightning (an idea: light only the face, while the rest of the money would be noticed, but still be in the dark). i wish you luck, because this is one of the photos that got the smallest score from me.</td>', '4 the only interesting thing about this photo is the depth of field, which doesn´t say much about the quality. not only that this is quite a boring photo of some money (what´s the point of this money being there? where did it come from? whose is it? - questions i´m not interested at all finding the answers), but even technically this photo leaves to be desired. i guess a way to improve it would be playing with colour and saturation, or having a less uniform and dull lightning (an idea: light only the face, while the rest of the money would be noticed, but still be in the dark). i wish you luck, because this is one of the photos that got the smallest score from me.', '2006-12-24 03:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(3145839, 440641, 48471, '<td valign="top">4 i guess you´re a victim of the limitations of your camera. i´m saying so, because i feel you wanted a macro shot of the eye, but ended up with this perfect-rule-of-the-thirds-shot, but nothing more. i think even digital zooming of the eye and some colour manipulations would result in a more interesting photo. good luck, although this photo gets the lowest score i vote on this challlenge.</td>', '4 i guess you´re a victim of the limitations of your camera. i´m saying so, because i feel you wanted a macro shot of the eye, but ended up with this perfect-rule-of-the-thirds-shot, but nothing more. i think even digital zooming of the eye and some colour manipulations would result in a more interesting photo. good luck, although this photo gets the lowest score i vote on this challlenge.', '2006-12-24 03:06:50.000000', NULL, 1),
