(3157340, 440026, 69350, '<td valign="top">I checked out most of your work and I love how you compose your photographs. <br/> <br/>I love the color, the DOF and the fact that your subject is on the right (my fave way of shooting things) for this one. <br/> <br/>Congrats on ur top 5 finish. :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-28 20:27:17.</i></td>', 'I checked out most of your work and I love how you compose your photographs.  I love the color, the DOF and the fact that your subject is on the right (my fave way of shooting things) for this one.  Congrats on ur top 5 finish. :)', '2006-12-28 20:26:30.000000', '2006-12-28 20:27:17.000000', 0),
(3157683, 440336, 62009, '<td valign="top">You know, this fits perfectly.  It''s a shame that you can''t see the photog''s notes prior to the finish of the challenge.  What goes from a bad shot with people wondering what the hell you were thinking to absolute clarity of an amazing shot just from your words.  I have to say that I''m one of those people who didn''t vote this higher, because I was wondering what you were thinking.  I have to apologize.  You hit it dead on!!!!</td>', 'You know, this fits perfectly.  It''s a shame that you can''t see the photog''s notes prior to the finish of the challenge.  What goes from a bad shot with people wondering what the hell you were thinking to absolute clarity of an amazing shot just from your words.  I have to say that I''m one of those people who didn''t vote this higher, because I was wondering what you were thinking.  I have to apologize.  You hit it dead on!!!!', '2006-12-28 22:47:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3157736, 439322, 50641, '<td valign="top">Great acting!  I love what your curves did to the sky.  DPC typically gets grouchy about weird contrast on people, unless it''s high key or grunge.  It stunk that this wasn''t an advanced challenge - because in that case you could have masked out your subject and had the effect in the sky only (as noraneko mentions).  However, given the extreme/surreal leanings of a PF challenge, you should have been given more leeway and scored higher.  Pffft.</td>', 'Great acting!  I love what your curves did to the sky.  DPC typically gets grouchy about weird contrast on people, unless it''s high key or grunge.  It stunk that this wasn''t an advanced challenge - because in that case you could have masked out your subject and had the effect in the sky only (as noraneko mentions).  However, given the extreme/surreal leanings of a PF challenge, you should have been given more leeway and scored higher.  Pffft.', '2006-12-28 23:05:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3157768, 440564, 50641, '<td valign="top">I thought this was a great wall shot.  It has a really harsh and desolate feel to it - perfect.  This is the kind of photo where I''d probably play with curves and levels for a while, then decide to leave it the way it was anyway ;-)</td>', 'I thought this was a great wall shot.  It has a really harsh and desolate feel to it - perfect.  This is the kind of photo where I''d probably play with curves and levels for a while, then decide to leave it the way it was anyway ;-)', '2006-12-28 23:11:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3157892, 440636, 50641, '<td valign="top">You executed the idea beautifully. I so love the blue sky behind the bowl and the upshot really works.  I also considered doing this for "our" lyric (rummaged through my brain for all sorts of souls - tissue paper, toile, dye, etc and then finally chickened out and drew them, which definitely had its problems).  I would have been very happy to have submitted this.</td>', 'You executed the idea beautifully. I so love the blue sky behind the bowl and the upshot really works.  I also considered doing this for "our" lyric (rummaged through my brain for all sorts of souls - tissue paper, toile, dye, etc and then finally chickened out and drew them, which definitely had its problems).  I would have been very happy to have submitted this.', '2006-12-28 23:58:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3158051, 440026, 69008, '<td valign="top">I''m glad that you went back for more. The frost and red in front of the green and brown background really make a scene worth looking at. Just lovely in color and composition, your usual fine eye for what makes an image shows again in this one.</td>', 'I''m glad that you went back for more. The frost and red in front of the green and brown background really make a scene worth looking at. Just lovely in color and composition, your usual fine eye for what makes an image shows again in this one.', '2006-12-29 00:32:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3158448, 440343, 18339, '<td valign="top">Congrats to you, well done:)</td>', 'Congrats to you, well done:)', '2006-12-29 02:44:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3158507, 440183, 70432, '<td valign="top">perfect, nice job.</td>', 'perfect, nice job.', '2006-12-29 03:54:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3158814, 440519, 64844, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for commenting! I really appreciate it!<br/>Yes, I did look up through thick glass walls and water and those fish kept moving in and out of the picture. Probably I should have chosen one of the sharper ones , bt with only one fish. <br/> <br/>I really liked the strange perspective of the fish floating above the viewer and realize that the photo is not much worth from a technical point of view or composition.<br/> <br/>Looking at the text of "Brain Damage" though, I thought it represented quite well that spongey dizzy feeling of somebody not able of a clear thought!</td>', 'Thank you all for commenting! I really appreciate it!Yes, I did look up through thick glass walls and water and those fish kept moving in and out of the picture. Probably I should have chosen one of the sharper ones , bt with only one fish.  I really liked the strange perspective of the fish floating above the viewer and realize that the photo is not much worth from a technical point of view or composition. Looking at the text of "Brain Damage" though, I thought it represented quite well that spongey dizzy feeling of somebody not able of a clear thought!', '2006-12-29 08:06:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3158861, 439227, 52467, '<td valign="top">So very cool...awesome work!</td>', 'So very cool...awesome work!', '2006-12-29 08:30:52.000000', NULL, 0),
