(3177285, 440548, 60862, '<td valign="top">Wow, what a powerful image!  Just ignore nitpicky people;  make a better gas mask?  Sheesh!<br/> <br/>Remember that you really can''t do anything with selection tools or brushes in basic.  Just stick to adjustment layers without layer masks.<br/> <br/>Don''t sweat it, though;  plenty of people make a simple mistake, learn from it, and live happily ever after. :)</td>', 'Wow, what a powerful image!  Just ignore nitpicky people;  make a better gas mask?  Sheesh! Remember that you really can''t do anything with selection tools or brushes in basic.  Just stick to adjustment layers without layer masks. Don''t sweat it, though;  plenty of people make a simple mistake, learn from it, and live happily ever after. :)', '2007-01-03 17:43:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3177640, 438284, 69700, '<td valign="top">Kelly,  Very nice photo.  I find this photo very intense and moody.  I was surprised that this was a self portrait.  You need to find some models so you can devote all your energy to one side of the camera.</td>', 'Kelly,  Very nice photo.  I find this photo very intense and moody.  I was surprised that this was a self portrait.  You need to find some models so you can devote all your energy to one side of the camera.', '2007-01-03 18:59:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3179160, 440539, 15358, '<td valign="top">well, this is a good lesson for me...<br/> <br/>I have always found Pink Floyd to be somewhat dark and edgy.  For me, I really wanted the clouds to be dark and maybe a bit ominous. Working in within basic rules I had to make some choices as to how the image would go.  Now, I know this background,  the vegetation on the hillsides is all very homogenous, seeing it in the foreground is basically the way it is on all the hillsides.  I worked hard to not have the shadow detail go completely black,  looking at the image for a few seconds,  you can see that the hillsides are very similar to the foreground, yet the clouds are making them very black, Will the dam break?  what sort of upheaval might be ready to happen that might cause a catastrophe?  <br/> <br/>Those were the sort of questions, feeling I was looking to evoke.  Thank you for all of the comments.</td>', 'well, this is a good lesson for me... I have always found Pink Floyd to be somewhat dark and edgy.  For me, I really wanted the clouds to be dark and maybe a bit ominous. Working in within basic rules I had to make some choices as to how the image would go.  Now, I know this background,  the vegetation on the hillsides is all very homogenous, seeing it in the foreground is basically the way it is on all the hillsides.  I worked hard to not have the shadow detail go completely black,  looking at the image for a few seconds,  you can see that the hillsides are very similar to the foreground, yet the clouds are making them very black, Will the dam break?  what sort of upheaval might be ready to happen that might cause a catastrophe?   Those were the sort of questions, feeling I was looking to evoke.  Thank you for all of the comments.', '2007-01-04 01:32:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(3180215, 440058, 18868, '<td valign="top">Hey there -- been busy, wanted to enter, just now looking at the entries.  Aweseome.  You were soooo robbed, should have been top 20, IMHO.  The reason for the score is evident by the comments -- the voters have obviously never seen the movie.  Good work!  Technically speaking, there''s a bit of "tungsten" color cast in the whites &amp; highlights that I might remove if it were my shot.</td>', 'Hey there -- been busy, wanted to enter, just now looking at the entries.  Aweseome.  You were soooo robbed, should have been top 20, IMHO.  The reason for the score is evident by the comments -- the voters have obviously never seen the movie.  Good work!  Technically speaking, there''s a bit of "tungsten" color cast in the whites & highlights that I might remove if it were my shot.', '2007-01-04 10:51:09.000000', NULL, 0),
